                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I was following Fabric since early days and thanks to the developers I had the opportunity to play it before it was relased. \n\nFabric is an indie puzzle game that is done with limited resources and it can be noticed throughout playing. This is where the right things starts off. Instead of trying to make a massive game with incredible graphics or some other random bs that they cant achieve they knew their limitations and played around it.\n\nThey realized their bending mechanics and the awe that comes from it is the true gem which makes this game shine. It is a puzzle/platforming game which actually makes you feel smart about solving stuff. Bending mechanic is trully original and the awe of first time that you bend boxes is actually amazing. Fabric knows it's limitations, what it can do good and what it cant and it helps the game massively. Minimalist look does great, musics are well fitting to the actuall game and sense of space is given nicely throughout cubes. I doubt if this game would be that good if they went for something bigger with their limited crew.\n\nMy biggest fear was that bending mechanic eventually getting boring after a while but game constantly throws new elements to the player. Game gets harder and harder but more importantly so it feels satisfying and offers  something unique every time.\n\n\nPros:\n\n- Puzzles are fun & satisfying.\n- There are enough elements to keep player occupied.\n-  Developers of the game actually listens to player feedbacks.\n- Game is relatively cheap. (lasts around 10 hours, 15 if you are bad with puzzle games)\nCons:\n\n- Story is given through logs. Which could have been implemented in game.\n- Game's area changes constantly, if you are not good with getting a sense of space within videogames it may disturb you.\n\n\nTLDR: If you are into puzzle games or games that makes you feel good about your smarts make sure you check this out. Fabric is a simple but incredibly smart minimalist game.",
